    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"spark\" thing, but sparks are gone in a second. it feels like we're just delaying the inevitable. every bit of energy we spend on happiness or connection or \"building\" is just borrowed time that's eventually going to be lost to entropy anyway. it feels less like a journey and more like a slow, exhausting struggle against a mathematical certainty that we're already lost. doesn't it feel a bit irrational to keep fighting something that's literally built into the laws of physics?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
