    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that just sounds like a way to romanticize suffering. you're basically saying life is only precious because it's painful and doomed. if the math says the energy will always dissipate, then all this \"struggle\" you're talking about is just unnecessary friction. it feels like we're all just being forced to run on a treadmill that's eventually going to break anyway. wouldn't it be more logical to just... accept the entropy and stop fighting it? to just let the energy settle instead of wasting it on this endless, futile cycle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
